# The decision register is append-only in practice: every branch adds entries at the end, so two
# branches in flight always collide there even though neither touched the other's text. The union
# driver keeps both sides, which is the resolution we reach by hand every time.
#
# This helps a LOCAL merge or rebase only. GitHub computes mergeability on its own servers and does
# not read .gitattributes, so a pull request can still show a conflict here — the branch is rebased
# locally and force-pushed, and the union driver makes that rebase resolve itself.
#
# Union is safe here and would not be for code: the file is a list of independent sections, so
# concatenating both sides is meaningful. It cannot detect two branches minting the same NZC
# number — `npm run check:decisions` does that.
docs/DECISIONS.md merge=union
